# Implementation Plan - EdLove Web Footer

## Goal Description
Implement a "premium" looking footer for the EdLove web application. This footer will serve as the navigational anchor for legal and informational pages ("About Us", "Privacy", "Terms of Use") and include a "Built with 💖" attribution, adhering to the project's cinematic and soulful aesthetic.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE] 
> I will be creating a new branch `feature/edlove-footer` from `main` before applying these changes.

## Proposed Changes

### apps/edlove-web/src/components

#### [NEW] [Footer.astro](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/edlove-web/src/components/Footer.astro)
- Create a new Astro component for the Footer.
- **Structure**:
  - Container with `deep-indigo` background (or similar dark theme color).
  - Grid layout for links:
    - **About Us**
    - **Privacy Policy**
    - **Terms of Use**
  - Bottom section for "Built with 💖" and copyright.
- **Styling**: Use Tailwind CSS to match the design system (fonts `Libre Baskerville` for headings, `Inter` for text).

### apps/edlove-web/src/layouts

#### [MODIFY] [Layout.astro](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/edlove-web/src/layouts/Layout.astro)
- Import `Footer` from `../components/Footer.astro`.
- Render `<Footer />` after the `<slot />` (main content).
- Ensure the main content takes up remaining height so the footer sits at the bottom (using `flex-col` and `min-h-screen` if not already present, or sticky footer).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run build` within `apps/edlove-web` to ensure no build errors.

### Manual Verification
- Start the dev server: `npm run dev`.
- Visually inspect the footer on the homepage.
- Check responsiveness (mobile/desktop).
- Verify all links are present (even if they point to `#` or separate pages for now).

